+---
+id: task-002-implement-json-patch-rfc-6902-applypatch
+type: task
+title: "Implement JSON Patch (RFC 6902) applyPatch"
+status: approved
+format: 1
+---
+
+# Request
+
+Implement JSON Patch per RFC 6902 and export `applyPatch(document, patch)` from `src/index.ts`, with the
+operations add, remove, replace, move, copy and test. It returns a new document without mutating its
+input, and throws when the patch is invalid or an operation fails.
+
+# Acceptance
+
+- RFC 6902 section 4 semantics for each operation, including `-` array append, index `== length` on add,
+  whole-document replacement with path `""`, and move/copy/test as specified (test uses JSON equality).
+- `move` from a location to one of its own children is an error; `from`/`path` use RFC 6901 syntax.
+- Invalid patches (not an array, unknown `op`, missing or mistyped members) throw.
+- Input is never mutated; `__proto__`/`constructor` keys cannot pollute prototypes. No runtime dependency.
+- Tests cover the RFC 6902 appendix A examples and error cases; README documents the function.
